# eoreader6.1 · kernel · turn 021
# Act: DEF−  (Alteration aimed at Ground)   Stance: Clearing   Site: Atmosphere
#
# The Significance triad's first operator, first use — and the pivot this
# kernel's entire GOAL.md has been building toward. NUL/SIG/INS (Existence)
# and SEG/CON/SYN (Structure) establish and relate FACTS: something exists,
# is named, is anchored, is bounded, is connected, is composed. None of
# them assert what a fact MEANS. DEF "establishes what holds within a
# stable interpretive frame" (EO Event Streaming §3) — the first operator
# whose job is interpretation rather than structure.
#
# Numbered 021, not 020: gap-020 already occupies that position in the
# sequence, refused. Turn numbering stays strictly monotonic regardless of
# earned/refused status, so position in the file order always matches
# position in time — a refusal still happened, even though it produced no
# register to open from.
#
# DEF− clears the atmosphere for interpretation: establishing that a FRAME
# exists — specifically the one GOAL.md names, "signal, not noise." Nothing
# is yet claimed about any entity within it; this turn only makes the
# frame available to claim within, the same grain SIG−, CON−, and SYN−
# each occupied before their own Figure-grain acts.
#
# Earning argument: precondition is having entities worth interpreting,
# which the Existence and Structure triads have supplied throughout
# (turn-12, turn-13's anchors, specifically, for what follows). Refuted if
# no stable frame could be named — GOAL.md names one directly.

:turn-21  eot:opens        :turn-19 .
:turn-21  eot:act          eot:DEF- .
:turn-21  eot:stance       "Clearing" .
:turn-21  eot:site         "Atmosphere" .
:turn-21  eot:frame        "signal, not noise (kernel/GOAL.md)" .
:turn-21  eot:closes       [ eot:aperture 1.0 ; eot:perturbation "none" ] .
